// endpoint_resolve_peer_delivery.proto — ResolvePeerDelivery: WHICH SESSION
// received one cross-session message, by the vendor's delivery id for it.
//
// WHY THE DAEMON ASKS A SHIM. The daemon draws the sender's row of a send to
// another Claude session and names the session the message reached. The
// delivery id is the one value both ends of the message share
// (conversation.v1.PeerDeliveryId), and the record that holds the delivered
// copy is in the host's one store, which the daemon never reads directly: its
// read path is this service. Any running shim can answer, because the store is
// shared by every session on the host; the shim asks the store and relays.

